{"author":{"id":"d4d77c46d796577aec35d160aa1e09aa095720b03e93f3ca34ad3c079140e2fb"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794731288,"nonce":"AoZrSs0/VXCcxyvP5eKE3pcp6xs=","message":"Design: targets. Covers this issue and a4978d99e7c95bdf75eb3ea95564c8da508c3f2fa39205fc43b0ad4e09cdf510 (fields).\n\nA target is what consumes a compiled shader: it reads russl's output, may run build steps, and adds fields to the class. Today's four field sets become four built-in targets, and a driver adds its own the way a framework adds an Extension. An Extension changes the language; a Target consumes the result. They stay separate classes.\n\n\n    class Target {\n        public final name:String;               // \"metal\"; unique per shader\n        public function new(name:String);\n        /** The russl outputs build() reads: Msl, Hlsl, Spirv, Glsl. */\n        public function needs():Array\u003cSource\u003e;\n        /** The fields this target adds to one shader class. */\n        public function build(shader:Compiled):Array\u003cField\u003e;\n    }\n\n    Targets.register(target, ?family)   // as Extensions.register: all shaders, or one family\n\n`Compiled` is one shader as the build has it:\n\n- `name`, `cls`, `pos`; `wgsl`; `layout` (the front end's WgslLayout); `constants` (the `@:constants` values);\n- `groups`, `entryPoints`: the LAYOUT and ENTRY_POINTS data;\n- `msl()`, `hlsl()`, `spirv()`, `glsl()`, `glslMissing()`, `native()`: the tool's output. Reading one a target did not list in `needs()` is a build error, so the tool runs only for shaders whose targets need it.\n- `step(key, inputs, run, outputs)`: a cached build step. `inputs` maps file names to bytes; hxnsl writes them to a cache directory, calls `run(dir)` (the target runs whatever process it needs), then reads `outputs`. Cached by target name, `key` and the inputs; `key` carries the external tool's version, which the target finds once (`xcrun metal --version`). A step that leaves an output missing fails the build, naming the target and the shader.\n- `resource(suffix, bytes)`: adds `hxnsl/\u003cclass\u003e/\u003ctarget\u003e/\u003csuffix\u003e` and returns the name.\n- `error(msg)`: fails the build at the shader, prefixed with the target's name.\n\nThe core fields stay with every shader regardless of targets: WGSL, HXSL's layout constants, LAYOUT, ENTRY_POINTS.\n\n\n- The targets registered for any of its families, deduplicated by name.\n- If none: the default set, `-D hxnsl_targets=...` when given, else the four built-ins. This is today's behaviour, so a program with no driver is unchanged.\n- `hxnsl_targets` names built-ins and registered targets alike; an unknown name is an error.\n- Two targets of one shader adding the same field fail the build, naming both.\n\nA driver that wants a built-in's fields as well registers it beside its own: `Targets.register(new hxnsl.targets.Msl(), \"gpu.metal.Shader\")`.\n\n\n`hxnsl.targets.Msl` (MSL, MSL_SLOTS), `Hlsl` (HLSL, HLSL_SLOTS), `Spirv` (spirv()), `Glsl` (GLSL_VERTEX, GLSL_FRAGMENT, GLSL_BINDINGS or GLSL_MISSING). The code moves out of Build.native unchanged; Build keeps the core fields, target selection and the tool run.\n\n\n    class MetalTarget extends hxnsl.Target {\n        public function new() super(\"metal\");\n        override function needs() return [Msl];\n        override function build(s:Compiled) {\n            var out = s.step(compilerVersion(), [\"shader.metal\" =\u003e Bytes.ofString(s.msl())], dir -\u003e {\n                run(\"xcrun\", [\"-sdk\", \"macosx\", \"metal\", \"-std=macos-metal2.1\", \"-c\", '$dir/shader.metal', \"-o\", '$dir/shader.air']);\n                run(\"xcrun\", [\"-sdk\", \"macosx\", \"metallib\", '$dir/shader.air', \"-o\", '$dir/shader.metallib']);\n            }, [\"shader.metallib\"]);\n            var res = s.resource(\"metallib\", out[\"shader.metallib\"]);\n            return (macro class {\n                public static function metallib():haxe.io.Bytes return haxe.Resource.getBytes($v{res});\n                public static final METAL_SLOTS = $v{...};\n            }).fields;\n        }\n    }\n\nregistered from hxn-gpu-metal's extraParams.hxml for its shader family. Where the host has no Metal compiler (a Linux build of an iOS app), the target decides: fail, or ship MSL for `newLibraryWithSource`. hxnsl does not choose.\n\n\n- 6230e8a6816b14cf7e92975eff31d177ad095a26b3c7671f703a6710de413ead (per-target extern bodies): the target's name is what the printer would key per-target bodies on. Compiled would then carry each target's own WGSL, and needs() would decide which ones the tool compiles. This design does not do it.\n- a4a79593c35cec91eb69a4fd17419a85a1e3b8eedd16fc77bea3623366e44676 (checks on the linked shader): a target can already reject a shader in build() with error(); the extension hook remains separate.\n- fd7f9c256112d3404ba3cf26d0ff4782114a2e4fe732761ae03ea0b92eb88f82 (@const variants): Compiled would become one per value set, and a target would build once for each.\n\n\ntest/framework registers a `probe` target for FrameworkShader that needs Spirv, runs a step in Haxe code (no external process) and adds a field from the step's output. Checks: Exposed has the probe's field and none of the built-ins' fields; Tinted, outside the family, keeps the four built-ins; two shaders with the same step inputs run the step once; a field clash and an unknown hxnsl_targets name fail the build with their messages.\n\nNot in scope: russl's per-target options (MSL version, shader model, SPIR-V flags), which are russl_compiler's.","files":null}]}